<% content_for :title, "Import polls · Admin · 535" %>

<h1 class="font-serif text-2xl font-semibold text-slate-900">Import polls from CSV</h1>
<p class="mt-1 text-sm text-slate-600">Every row goes through the same <code>Ingest::RecordPoll</code> door as manual entry and the scraper (entry mode "csv"). One bad row does not stop the rest of the file — each row's outcome is reported separately.</p>

<%= form_with url: admin_poll_imports_path, method: :post, multipart: true, class: "mt-6 rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5", data: { testid: "admin-poll-import-form" } do %>
  <label class="block text-sm font-medium text-slate-700" for="file">CSV file</label>
  <input type="file" name="file" id="file" accept=".csv,text/csv" required class="mt-2 block text-sm" data-testid="admin-poll-import-file-input">
  <%= submit_tag "Upload and import", class: "mt-4 cursor-pointer rounded-md bg-slate-900 px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-white hover:bg-slate-700", data: { testid: "admin-poll-import-submit" } %>
<% end %>

<section class="mt-8 rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-5 text-sm text-slate-700" data-testid="admin-poll-import-docs">
  <h2 class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-slate-500">Column format</h2>
  <p class="mt-2">First row is the header. Columns, in order:</p>
  <table class="mt-3 w-full max-w-3xl text-left text-xs">
    <thead class="text-slate-500"><tr><th class="py-1 pr-3 font-medium">Column</th><th class="py-1 font-medium">Meaning</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-200">
      <tr><td class="py-1 pr-3 font-mono">race_slug</td><td class="py-1">A race's slug (see the Races page), or blank for a generic-ballot poll.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="py-1 pr-3 font-mono">pollster</td><td class="py-1">Free text — matched to an existing pollster by canonicalized name.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="py-1 pr-3 font-mono">field_start</td><td class="py-1">YYYY-MM-DD, optional.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="py-1 pr-3 font-mono">field_end</td><td class="py-1">YYYY-MM-DD, required.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="py-1 pr-3 font-mono">sample_size</td><td class="py-1">Integer, optional.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="py-1 pr-3 font-mono">population</td><td class="py-1">One of lv / rv / a / unknown (case-insensitive), optional.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="py-1 pr-3 font-mono">sponsor</td><td class="py-1">Free text, optional.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="py-1 pr-3 font-mono">source_url</td><td class="py-1">Required.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="py-1 pr-3 font-mono">dem_pct, rep_pct</td><td class="py-1">Required result percentages.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="py-1 pr-3 font-mono">ind_pct, other_pct</td><td class="py-1">Optional result percentages.</td></tr>
      <tr><td class="py-1 pr-3 font-mono">dem_candidate, rep_candidate, ind_candidate</td><td class="py-1">Optional — a candidate's name within that row's race, matched exactly. No "other_candidate" column.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="mt-3">A blank percentage means that party has no result on that poll — leave <code>ind_pct</code>/<code>other_pct</code> empty for most races. Whole-file transactionality is not the contract: every row is recorded independently, and one row's rejection never affects another's.</p>
</section>
